    a: "<b>Centor Score Calculation (4 points):</b><ul><li>Tonsillar exudates (<b>+1</b>), Tender cervical nodes (<b>+1</b>), Fever history (<b>+1</b>), Absence of cough (<b>+1</b>)</li></ul><br><b>Management Algorithm based on Centor Score:</b><ol><li><b>Score &le; 1:</b> Low risk (&lt; 10%). <b>Symptomatic therapy</b>; no testing or antibiotics.</li><li><b>Score 2–3:</b> Intermediate risk (15–35%). Perform a <b>rapid antigen detection test (RADT)</b>. If positive, treat with antibiotics. If negative, obtain throat culture in children (adults do not require culture).</li><li><b>Score &ge; 4:</b> High risk (&gt; 50%). Perform **RADT** and treat only if positive (current guidelines recommend testing first; empiric antibiotics are rarely indicated unless testing is unavailable).</li></ol>"
