    a: "<b>Proteinuria Initial Diagnostic Algorithm:</b><ol><li>Confirm dipstick proteinuria (which primarily detects <b>albumin</b>) by obtaining a quantitative measurement: a random <b>spot urine protein-to-creatinine ratio (UPCR)</b> or a <b>spot urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio (UACR)</b>.</li><li>Define severity:</li><ul><li><b>Normal:</b> UPCR &lt; 150 mg/g (UACR &lt; 30 mg/g)</li><li><b>Microalbuminuria (moderately increased):</b> UACR <b>30–300 mg/g</b></li><li><b>Macroalbuminuria (severely increased):</b> UACR <b>&gt; 300 mg/g</b> or UPCR &gt; 300 mg/g</li><li><b>Nephrotic range:</b> UPCR <b>&gt; 3.5 g/day</b> (3500 mg/g)</li></ul></ol>"
