    a: "<b>Evaluation of Confirmed Proteinuria:</b><ol><li><b>Exclude transient proteinuria:</b> Caused by fever, exercise, CHF, acute illness, or seizure. Repeat the urine test on a separate day when the stressor is resolved.</li><li><b>Rule out Orthostatic Proteinuria:</b> Common in adolescents. Obtain a <b>split urine collection</b>: first morning void (while recumbent) vs. daytime void (while upright).</li></ol><b>Resolution:</b> The diagnosis is **orthostatic proteinuria** (benign condition; no further treatment or diagnostic evaluation is needed)."
