    a: "<b>Hepatobiliary ALP Workup Algorithm:</b><ol><li>Perform a **Right Upper Quadrant (RUQ) abdominal ultrasound** to evaluate the biliary tree.</li><li>If ducts are non-dilated (rules out extrahepatic obstruction like choledocholithiasis or mass), check **Antimitochondrial Antibodies (AMA)**:</li><ul><li><b>AMA Positive:</b> Diagnosis is likely **Primary Biliary Cholangitis (PBC)**. Treat with **ursodeoxycholic acid**.</li><li><b>AMA Negative:</b> Obtain an **MRCP** to evaluate for **Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC)** (beaded appearance of bile ducts) or consider liver biopsy for infiltrative disorders.</li></ul></ol>"
