    a: "<b>Secondary Hypertension Workup Algorithm:</b><ol><li>**Screening Indications:** Early onset (&lt; 30 years) without family history, late onset (&gt; 55 years), resistant HTN (&ge; 3 drugs at optimal doses including a diuretic), or sudden loss of BP control.</li><li>**Work up specific etiologies based on clinical clues:**</li><ul><li>**Renal Artery Stenosis:** Renal bruit, sudden creatinine rise &gt; 30% after starting ACEi. Screen with **renal duplex ultrasound** or CTA/MRA.</li><li>**Primary Aldosteronism:** Hypokalemia, drug-resistant HTN. Screen with **aldosterone-to-renin ratio (ARR)**.</li><li>**Pheochromocytoma:** Paroxysmal HTN, headache, palpitations, diaphoresis. Screen with **plasma free metanephrines** or 24-hr urine metanephrines.</li><li>**Cushing Syndrome:** Cushingoid features, striae. Screen with **LDDST** or **24-hr UFC**.</li><li>**Coarctation of the Aorta:** BP discrepancy between arms/legs, rib notching. Screen with **echocardiogram**.</li><li>**Obstructive Sleep Apnea (OSA):** Snoring, daytime somnolence. Screen with **polysomnography**.</li></ul></ol>"
